From 0a48a18f47dbd3ac9ee59467c75bdff7cfb94f3f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 00:07:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Layout of the arrays of the material data managers

The initializer of a material data manager chooses the layout of its
arrays: point by point (default) or component by component. Everything
given at each point follows it: states, tangent operator blocks, inputs of
the initialize functions, outputs of the post-processings, external state
variables with several components. Views on the arrays in the layout of
the manager (getGradientsView, getGradientView, getTangentOperatorBlockView,
etc.). The deformation gradient is set to the identity, the internal state
variables are extracted and the finite strain outputs are converted with
the strides of the layout (also on material data views). updateValues
checks that both states have the same layout. Material function managers
accept an initializer; their views stored point by point also accept the
scalar variables of a manager stored component by component, and new
accessors give views with a strided coalesced memory access. Conversions
of the views of mgis::function to field views.
